# --- Evidence and derived artifacts ---
# Working copies, carved files, decoded output and session logs are produced by
# running the analysis; they are reproducible from the register and must not be
# committed. Manual §9 also forbids overwriting them, which git would do on a
# merge. The register itself IS committed -- it is the report's backbone.
# results/ is scratch: working copies, carving output, session logs. Recovered
# evidence does NOT live here -- it goes in lab*/evidence/, which is committed,
# because the report states each artifact's SHA-256 and the ZIP must contain
# that exact file. Regenerating artifacts on another machine risks a different
# hash, and we are deliberately not all on the same environment.
#
# Session logs stay out on purpose: a typescript is where a recovered password
# ends up (§8). Review one before it goes in the ZIP.
lab*/results/*
!lab*/results/.gitkeep
!lab*/results/artifact-register.md
!lab*/results/environment-and-tools*.txt
!lab*/results/INVESTIGATION-GUIDE.md
!lab*/results/artifact-register.md
# Scripts are auxiliary deliverables and the group has to share them.
!lab*/results/scripts/

# Material handed out by the teaching team (pcaps, TLS key logs): kept
# read-only in lab*/artifacts/, referenced by SHA-256, never committed
# (t2.pcapng alone is >100MB, and key logs decrypt the whole capture).
lab*/artifacts/*
!lab*/artifacts/.gitkeep
!lab*/artifacts/SHA256SUMS
*.pcapng
*.keys

# Disk/memory images live in lab*/images/ (mounted at /work/lab*/images).
lab*/images/*
!lab*/images/.gitkeep

# Disk and memory images. These reach GB scale and github rejects >100MB.
*.dd
*.raw
*.img
*.E01
*.Ex01
*.aff4
*.vmem
*.mem
*.lime
*.pcapng.gz

# Recovered passwords and John state -- Manual §8.
*.pot
.john/

# --- LaTeX build output ---
*.aux
*.bbl
*.blg
*.fdb_latexmk
*.fls
*.lof
*.log
*.lot
*.out
*.synctex.gz
*.toc
main.pdf

# --- OS junk ---
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
Thumbs.db

# --- Editor / scratch ---
.idea/
*.swp
*~
scratch/
*.tmp
